[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 359,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55873,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plexiform fibromyxoma is a benign mesenchymal neoplasm that arises in the antrum and pyloric region.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 360,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55874,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8811/0 Plexiform fibromyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 361,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55875,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 161,
        "headingText": "<p>2E92.1 Benign neoplasm of stomach</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-05-03T10:07:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 362,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55876,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> plexiform angiomyxoid myofibroblastic tumour of the stomach.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 363,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55877,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 364,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55878,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plexiform fibromyxoma is primarily gastric, but the duodenum can be involved.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 365,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55879,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Presenting symptoms include gastrointestinal bleeding, ulcer, weight loss, and pyloric obstruction.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 366,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55880,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Males and females are affected equally, and tumours have been reported over a wide patient age distribution, including in childhood.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 367,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55881,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 368,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55882,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrent <em>MALAT1</em>-<em>GLI1</em> fusions and <em>GLI1</em> polysomy have been identified in a subset of tumours that show GLI1 overexpression {27101025}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 375,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 207,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55883,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 207,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours form gelatinous or haemorrhagic multinodular masses of 3&ndash;15&nbsp;cm (median: 5.5&nbsp;cm), sometimes protruding from the serosa {20556828; 19675452} but centred in the muscularis propria. Extension into the mucosa with associated ulceration is noted in a subset of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 369,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55884,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 169,
        "headingText": "<p>The nodules are composed of bland spindle cells, probably myofibroblasts, set in a myxoid, fibromyxoid, or collagenous matrix with a prominent arborizing thin-walled capillary network. Increased cellularity may be seen in tumours in the duodenal bulb or with extramural extension. Tumour nodules may extend into veins, which is of no clinical significance {19675452}. Substantial cytological atypia is absent, and the mitotic count is low (median: 1&nbsp;mitosis/10&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>) {19675452}. The spindle cells are positive for SMA and occasionally for desmin, whereas ALK, CD34, keratins, KIT, and DOG1 are negative {19675452; 20556828}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-06T11:06:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 370,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55885,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 371,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55886,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 374,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55887,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> multinodular and plexiform low-power architecture; uniform spindle cells in a myxoid, fibromyxoid, or collagenous stroma; delicate arborizing vasculature.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 372,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55888,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 373,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55889,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 195,
        "headingId": 173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plexiform fibromyxomas are benign, with no reports of recurrence or metastasis {17460456; 20556828; 19675452}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-15T16:19:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]